  "prefLabel": "Ins 1902.14 Prohibition Against Preexisting Conditions, Waiting Periods, Elimination Periods and Probationary Periods in Replacement Policies or Certificates",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 1902.14 Prohibition Against Preexisting Conditions, Waiting Periods, Elimination Periods and Probationary Periods in Replacement Policies or Certificates. If a Medicare supplement policy or certificate replaces another Medicare supplement policy or certificate, the replacing insurer shall waive any time periods applicable to preexisting conditions, waiting periods, elimination periods, and probationary periods in the new Medicare supplement policy for similar benefits to the extent such time was spent under the original policy.\n\nSource. #5119, eff 4-25-91; ss by #5656, eff 7-1-93; ss by #7017, INTERIM, eff 7-1-99, EXPIRED: 10-29-99\n\nNew. #8555, eff 2-1-06, EXPIRED: 2-1-14\n\nNew. #11014, eff 1-8-16; ss by #14661, eff 7-23-26, EXPIRES: 7-23-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins1900.html"
